<<~ ahu #/cold-start>>

!! Cold start

# `export LAR_ROOT=/tmp/lar-scratch-<you>` before any in-tree boot or store-touching `lares` command — `LAR_ROOT` moves the store, the bags root and every projection mirror root; `LAR_BAGS` alone moves only the bags root, and the projection still writes the tracked `bags/` and `wikis/`. A bare in-tree boot writes into the tracked tree, and `tools/tree-clean-witness.sh` reads that as red. The staged e2e set takes a scratch `LAR_ROOT` per vessel and NO global `LAR_BAGS`. A single `lares meme normalize|check` reads files and needs only a scratch `LAR_BAGS`.
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, then `pnpm -r build`, then `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:tw5-vendor` (the TW5 core blob `head-parity` and `scripts/smoke-plugin-boot.ts` need — `pnpm -r build` does not produce it), then `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`.
# A fresh `git worktree` holds empty submodules (`TiddlyWiki5`, `VSCode-TW5-Syntax`, `mempalace`); populate them before building there.
# `lares-cli` `tests/pour-repave.test.ts` needs the dev-root marker (`LAR_DEV_REPO_ROOT=1` or the gitignored `lar-dev-root.json`).
# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) rides in git and must equal a fresh build — rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it.
# Run `bash tools/witness-all.sh` for the whole fleet — a hand-picked subset of witnesses reads greener than the tree.
# Read `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot` (the boot seed), then this carrier, then the rulings memory (`project_grammar_as_tiddlers_rulings.md`) before touching grammar, frame, or ingest code.

