<<~ ahu #/wounds>>

!! Open wounds, ranked

The hosted walk, its cleanup and its aftermath stand, the three B1 rulings enacted (the worn face hosts; a herm answers the knock; a boot follows `LAR_ROOT`). Nothing below blocks a push; the rulings owed read in ''Pending operator rulings''.

''Landed in the round 6-f/6-g sweep'': the H1 one-holder law; the H2 VK commitment; the custody-root brand; the harness S1 items; genesis catch-up (`099f2bd42`); the `actorSeed` kupono law (`f04b82899`); and the engine on TW5 `develop` (`f04b82899`). These close their wounds; the R-ENGINE streams and plugins rulings remain recorded on the founding road.

# ''THE RE-FOUND, one train'' — the rulings that shape it, the slices in dependency order, and the questions the operator still owns read in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road`. It mints unversioned names, re-mints the engine and edge, and re-seats the Nexus; DESTROY-class strings stay frozen. The train: R-STORE ‖ R-CUSTODY → R-CHARTER (the one AID train, the Stable founding act inside it) → R-WIRE → R-ENGINE · R-EMBER · R-KAHU.
## ''No pave or wipe command'' (operator-ruled; such a command is too risky). A fresh START runs BY HAND: move the old homes aside — rename, never delete, so it stays reversible — then found fresh. Valuable data lives in git, in the private `claude-backup` repository, or on `D:` (`stable-founding-road#/fresh-start`).
## ''The live-holder gap'': `lares host` and `lares walk` route through the standing vessel's one store door; the remaining direct-store writers route in R-STORE.
# ''Beside the train, landed'': leaf↔leaf sync through a herm, session-bound (`identity-slot-policy#/the-leaf-taxonomy`), and the held-out dispatch driven from a host-built dist with `vessel found` on the runner — neither rides the train any longer; see `stable-founding-road#/the-road`.

''Carried, unranked''
* Road (iv): surface-for-review.
* Q6: loans keyed by CID.
* A design call on `/cas` timing; whether the parallel-draft alert persists.
* `packages/lararium-sensorium/requirements.txt` calls the tree-sitter versions one (Python binding 0.26, CLI 0.27; both ABI 15).

''Pending operator rulings''
* ''The road's open questions'' — `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/open`: the seal-roll successor's name; a root-holding browser leaf's backup slot; the seat's cold next key at founding; a sealed receipt manifest for carriage; carriage across leaves. (The projection's mirror root under `LAR_BAGS` stands ruled: the instruction names `LAR_ROOT`, `c86411102`.)
* ''The two-voice herm'' (research done): may a herm speak in a voice of its own, or only through a share of one? `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lamplighters#/open` strikes `operate ⊥ sign` and proposes a FROST Place-DID with the herm holding one share; its drift-ward splits the utterances — federation-facing and condemnation-relevant ones thresholded, local carry single-signed — and `#/immune`'s "herms present" (the victim testifies) reads beside "the least credible witness to its own neglect". The split stands as the ruling owed.
* ''The Lamplighters' question'': whether island-admin tending (`tend.repair`) reaches the herm's own `@daemon` signing key — ISOLATE it, or ACCEPT it and price the lost independent testimony (`lamplighters#/open`; its `role` line advertises it).
* ''Two Kairoses'': the fiction's KAIROS watches the noosphere across nodes and speaks unasked (`elyncia/Elyncia_02_The_Lares_DreamNet.md`); the code's Kairos names, as a pet-name, an unbuilt OAuth-refresh entity that waits for the right moment (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/reach-plane`). One entity, or two that share a name?
* ''The `?` and the unechoed gate key'' — ruled DISTINCT, related only through THR_1. The frame's `from="?"` and `-> to="?"` declare an UNRESOLVED bearing — the carrier's origin and next hop stand unknown, and authorship rides inside the checked span (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext-framing#/bearing-arrow`). The gate's `lar:challenge` withholds a known key — the dialer verifies against its own pin, and an echoed key would confirm the gate to a replayer (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/auth-wire.ts`, `LarChallengeMsg`). One declares ignorance at the grammar layer; the other withholds knowledge at the transport layer. Neither cites the other; both stand as outward faces in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/system-pattern-integrities#/threshold-pattern-integrities` (the carrier row and the gate row), which carries their only shared law. R-WIRE retires the challenge (Noise IK `<- s`: the responder's key never rides the wire), so a direct citation would anchor on a deleted interface.
* ''The Codex crew's forks'', reconciled against the code in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/crew-handoff-codex#/reconciled`: the Offering Antigen scope (and the charter-inception identity it rests on); the crossing record's emission threshold and destination receipts; seam (b)'s altitude; `bag-residency.ts`'s home.

''Needs the operator''
* ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
* ''The offering's `offer`/`witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
* ''Engine cadence, still open'' (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu` `#/contract`): who holds a cadence share; one daemon hosting two engine epochs; whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds.
* ''Backstop seam (b), PHASE 5'' (`tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`): three child-edit shapes the test marks as the operator's call.
* ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`'s header): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph` (canon memes pin their mesh `source-file`), `pronaos`, `offering-inspection` (own mesh-namespace memes). Each moves or stays only by ruling.
* ''The capture cell'' sits isolated for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`, the sensorium-machina S5 ruling) places capture in Python per stream with the TS @daemon coordinating only; the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.

''Deferred by law or by the operator''
* ''The Sensorium's logic'' (`packages/lararium-sensorium/**`, tw5 `form-layer/**`, mesh `ffz-project`, `clock-recovery`, coupling/metric modules): the measure-servo aliases in `ffz-project.ts`, one five-band ladder (Title case `ApertureBand`, the others derived), the `lar_feedback` output field name. Frames inside it stay in scope for healing at any time.
* ''Tangle, the putback law, the tongue fold'' — gated on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` (mirror pairing, round-trip CI, Markdown injection into `hana`). The aka/weave rhyme (`memetic-wikitext-framing.mem` Annex) waits on tangle.
* ''A relay-stream profile'' — a stream of carriers belongs to the SYN-framed profile (`&#x0016;`, held in reserve); one `.mem` file frames one carrier. The profile defines batch framing and resynchronisation.
* ''A carrier seal'' — re-mint an attestation mark with a computed, verified check when signing lands.
* ''EOT targeting'' — what a resolved `-> to=` would name (the declared-unresolved meaning stands).
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' (build every package from clean, run every witness and suite) — run as a spirit pass, not built into the CLI or a trigger.

