<<~ ahu #/standing-law>>

!! Standing law that bites (read the canon before arguing with it)

* ''The frame stands as canon'': `@lararium/memetic-frame` — DOCTYPE → `<<^ code="&#x0001;" from="?" -> to="…">>` → `<<^ code="&#x0002;">>` → `toml meta` first in the body → body → `<<^ code="&#x0003;">>ni:///sha-256;…` → `<<^ code="&#x0004;" -> to="?">>`. Marks: SOH, SOH2 (the one kapu alias), STX, ETX, EOT; each declares its family. One span: first masked STX to first masked ETX; a second reads as a fault. A spelling outside the frame grammar tears the frame. See `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext-framing`.
* ''Ingest'' = decide(parse, verdict). The deserializer stands as the pure meme→tiddlers function; `verdict()` (Match · Stale · Absent · Torn · Bare) lives in the frame package; checks live in `carrier-check.ts`, composed by the ingest gate; repairs live in normalize; policy lives at each door. A stale check on a human edit warns; a torn frame refuses; text with no frame reads as bare data, UNSTABLE, never a meme.
* ''Never refuse on the stock syncer path''; surface on the alert rail instead.
* ''The quoteblock floor'' fences at two grains — the whole chunk inside the deserializer, so every door fences, and a child's body in place at the backstop's child gate: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ahu#/quoteblock-floor`.
* ''An admit carries across a seal roll only through its roll anchors''; the gate reads the presented admit against the carriage board's counted revokes and the kapae antigen, folding no allow roster; the board itself carries admits, roll anchors and hosting acts (the antigen's ALLOW-twin), one presenter reads it, and the anchors reach the verifier inside the presentation's lineage.
* ''Fragments'': every `lar:` fragment roots at `#/…`, one raw `#`, slot names `[a-z0-9āēīōūʻ-]`, `/` nests, `$` reserved; fragment law lives in the media type (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext`).
* ''Grammar lives in the tiddlers'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-*.tid` → `grammar-table.generated.ts`); sigil heads stay core ASCII; `aka` = informative pin, `kanawai` = binding pin, `kahea` = live transclusion; HUD gauges `aperture` and `ooda-ha`.
* ''Early alpha'': no back-compat, no shims, no legacy recovery — align stale things to the current frame and grammar. Derive, don't enumerate. Beware overcollapse: one function, one relation.
* ''Shared tree'': never `git stash`; commit only your paths with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`; never `--no-verify`; spirits never spawn helpers and never juggle another's uncommitted hunks; exit codes read directly, never through a pipe; a known positive proves a zero.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/map-ahead>>

!! Map ahead

# Work `#/wounds` in its order: the re-found first, then the lanes beside it. Bring the pending rulings to the operator before any lane builds against one.
# Walk the road at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-road`: R-STORE ‖ R-CUSTODY → R-CHARTER → R-WIRE → R-ENGINE · R-EMBER · R-KAHU. The device edge commits to the Nexus AID and `epoch0-<sha>` names become `nexus-<sha>` inside R-CHARTER; the engine-offer lineage and the engine fold (TW5 core plus the memetic-wikitext bootstrap into `engineCid`, the vocabulary leaving the engine as content) ride R-ENGINE.
# Exercise the quoteblock floor (both grains), the child gate and the persisted parallel drafts in the live wiki, against real concurrent browser saves, and turn every surprise into a test.
# The faces stand in canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine` `#/the-two-stacks`): end user `walk`; Lamplighter `carry`, `tend/island`, `tend/reach`; Kahu, the Nexus-scale `quorum-share`, its engine cadence a separate joint and the corpus-kahu at DreamNet scale; Guardian, the reserve share. Founding acts; it never stands as a face. Stacks compose on a persona, combined by default and split only by the holder's own act. Grammar per Nexus stands ruled: the grammar lives, the corpus-kahu curate it, and no version names it. The target scale model is the small clan.
# Rule the capture cell; then pick up the Sensorium's logic when the operator returns to it.
# Regenerate the tree-sitter grammar whole against the released TW5-Syntax 3.0.0 (the submodule pointer reads `4afa852`) — the regeneration unlocks tangle and the publication track.
# Publication: the `text/markdown; variant=memetic-markdown` registration, the provisional `lar` scheme (after `lar-uri` gains its Security section), the vnd./prs. media type, and `draft-fontany-*` / `draft-tiddlywiki-*` (the TW5 pairs move to kramdown-rfc2629 when the community walk begins). The standalone `$:/plugins/lares/memetic-wikitext` artifact ships from `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/standalone/`.

